course: dictionary
lesson: 5283
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Julian can mean more than one thing, so context tells you which one you need. A capital J is a clue: Julian is a boy's name, and the Famous Five books tell us Julian is the eldest child.
explain: When Julian describes a thing, it is about Julius Caesar. «The "Old New Year" on 14 January is 1 January in the old Julian calendar.» The words calendar and January show that Julian means the calendar Caesar brought in.
explain: Julian can also be a woman's name: Julian of Norwich was an English woman who wrote about God's love. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a person, or about time? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Julian is a name, and a capital letter is a clue that it means a person, such as Julian in the Famous Five.
fact: Julian of Norwich was an English woman who wrote about God's love.
fact: «Julian» can describe a calendar: the Julian calendar was brought in by Julius Caesar.
fact: The Julian calendar had 365 days and a leap day every 4 years, but its year was about 11 minutes too long, so it added up to about one whole day every 130 years.
fact: Some Orthodox Christians, for example in parts of Ukraine and Russia, still keep certain feasts by the Julian calendar, so their Christmas falls later.
exercise: «Julian is the eldest child in the Famous Five books.» What does Julian mean here? | Julius Caesar's calendar | A river in Norwich | A kind of food | *A boy's name
exercise: «The "Old New Year" on 14 January is 1 January in the old Julian calendar.» What is the Julian calendar? | *A calendar that Julius Caesar brought in | A name for January | A clock for the kitchen | A map of England
exercise: «Julian of Norwich wrote about God's love.» What is Julian in this sentence? | A calendar | A type of ship | A day of the week | *A woman's name
test: «The Julian year was about 11 minutes too long.» In this sentence, Julian means | A woman who wrote about God's love | A kind of bird | *To do with the calendar Caesar brought in | A boy's name
test: In old papers, «O.S.» means old style. Which calendar does O.S. point to? | A calendar with 400 days | A Famous Five book | *The Julian calendar | The Gregorian calendar we use today
exam: «Julian wrote about God's love in the 1300s.» Which meaning fits best? | A boy in the Famous Five | A calendar from ancient Rome | A word meaning very old | *A woman's name, Julian of Norwich
